x01-core-alignment patch 04-substep-count (git apply ignores this header)

E7 item: (a) Substep count.

SAGE26 behaviour (R/src/core_build_model.c:414-470): halo_age = Age[halo_snapnum] (:414);
deltaT_total = Age[galaxies[0].SnapNum] - halo_age (:420), from the workspace's first galaxy;
t_dyn = (galaxies[centralgal].Rvir / (galaxies[centralgal].Vvir + 1e-10)) * KM_PER_MPC /
UnitTime_in_s (:430-431), the central's stored post-join Rvir and Vvir, KM_PER_MPC = 3.086e19
(:81); with SubstepResolution 1.0 (the default, R/src/core_read_parameter_file.c:110; R0.par does
not set it) floor_steps = (int)ceil(STEPS * 1 - 1e-9) = 10 and cap_steps = (int)ceil(MAX_STEPS * 1
- 1e-9) = 30 (:443-447; STEPS 10 and MAX_STEPS 30 at R/src/macros.h:17-18); N = floor_steps, then
if t_dyn > 0, needed = (int)ceil(floor_steps * (deltaT_total / t_dyn)) replaces N when larger
(:449-455); then N = min(N, cap_steps) (:457-459); the substep loop runs N times (:470).

Mimic behaviour replaced: setup_module_context() (src/core/halo_evolution.c:175-183) sets
num_substeps to the run file's fixed SubSteps: 10 (models/sage26/input/sage26_mini-millennium.yaml:15;
TimestepScheme is not set, so the fixed scheme applies), or under TimestepScheme dynamic to
compute_dynamic_substeps() (src/core/timestep.c:11-27) of the central's interval and the raw
halo's Rvir/Vvir with a different formula and cap.

What the patch changes: num_substeps is computed by SAGE26's rule in setup_module_context(), with
deltaT_total from workspace[0].SnapNum (the progenitor snapshot the row still carries) and t_dyn from
the central row's stored Rvir and Vvir (doubles; their float storage is item b), whatever
TimestepScheme and SubSteps say. The package reads the count only through ctx->num_substeps and maps
substeps to its 10 history bins with SAGE26's (step * STEPS) / N (models/sage26/shared/
sage_sfr_history.h:130-139), so it accepts N up to 30. ctx->time_interval and substep_dt are unchanged.

Reading for i02: yes, it would change sage16's output (its substep count would no longer be the run
file's SubSteps wherever SAGE26's rule gives more than 10); halos-only has no substep physics, so
its output would not change.

diff --git a/src/core/halo_evolution.c b/src/core/halo_evolution.c
index d21b691c..abc15917 100644
--- a/src/core/halo_evolution.c
+++ b/src/core/halo_evolution.c
